Done — `f35d814`. The module-standard section gained a fourth bullet, **Generic typing**, explicitly framed as *the part that makes this the full canonical example* — the layer the non-generic field examples never exercise:

- `Reactive()` returns the same constructor but its return type can't carry `<T>` (TypeScript has no higher-kinded types), so `Class` casts back to the raw constructor type to keep `new VirtualScroller.Class<T>()` fully generic;
- `Instance<T>` applies `ReactiveInstance` by hand for the same reason;
- `Props<T>` grafts the parameter back over the one prop a runtime map can't type — the `Omit<…> & { modelValue: T[] }` move;
- `Exposed<T>` closes the loop for template refs.

And the SFC paragraph now shows the generic wiring itself — `<script setup generic="T extends BaseItem">` with the single `as unknown as VirtualScroller.Props<T>` cast, presented as recovering exactly the precision the runtime object can't carry. The frontmatter description ends with "generic typing included," and the page's OG banner was re-rendered since the description changed.

The example-page hierarchy is now cleanly stated across the set: fields = tier-2 contracts + runner extension, horizontal scroller = the complete standard *including* the generic layer.

